        <groundspeak:log id="705156571">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-07-25T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1685537">nosweat6060</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP639 Maker's Madness Flash Cap [FOUND]

This was my first visit to Nose Hill. I was impressed with the trail system and used my Montana 600 in automobile mode to follow the major paths. Neat. I was able to find 4 of the 6 brass caps that I was searching for. Thanks to ofth and vdD for setting this up, and maintaining it. This was find #2.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684182634">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="265062">nicolo</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP639 - Makers' Madness Flash Cap

N 51° 06.661 W 114° 05.881&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My last unfound Brass Cap in Calgary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A little more up and down to this cap from &quot;Nose Hill View&quot; but it was fun.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Overshot my down/up hill run and had to backtrack a bit. Found the Cap quickly, a few snaps and I was headed back to my Jeep. Managed to snag a coupla traditional caches on the way back.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
